sImJhc2VsaW5lIjoxOH1d]\n\n**Key Considerations**:\n- *Cutting* reduces \
resolution, so we use exponential decay to avoid artifacts\n- We wrap \
everything with `Manipulate` to interactively tune the parameters\n\nTest \
spectrum processing will follow:", "Display" -> "codemirror", 
    "Hash" -> "563c9926-d300-4bcd-8ea1-f35144ef7686", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"Hidden" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "62ec207b-e884-499a-bcbc-79381cfa3d79"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "# TDS: Interactive Signal Processing\n\n> It is common in \
time-domain spectroscopy to observe copies of the initial system response due \
to impedance mismatch. If deconvolution is not possible using slab-like \
models, then we have to smoothly suppress them to avoid artifacts in further \
processing.\n\nWe perform a 'surgery' by applying an envelope function to the \
signal to suppress echoes, which cause oscillations in the frequency \
domain:\n\n\n<div class=\"text-center w-full\"><svg version=\"1.1\" \
xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 918 286.86328125\">\n  \
