2</text></g></svg></div>\n\n\n**Key Considerations**:\n- *Cutting* reduces \
resolution, so we use exponential decay to avoid artifacts\n- We wrap \
everything with `Manipulate` to interactively tune the parameters\n\nTest \
spectrum processing will follow:", "Display" -> "markdown", 
    "Hash" -> "c328a10d-0197-454e-9a6d-c3c5ee1e8b82", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "62ec207b-e884-499a-bcbc-79381cfa3d79"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "test = NotebookRead@NotebookStore[\"troubling-fd8\"];\n\n{\n  \
ListLinePlot[test, ImageSize->400, PlotRange->Full, PlotLabel->\"Time \
domain\"], \n  ListLinePlot[Take[Fourier[test[[All,2]]], 500] // Abs, \
ImageSize->400, PlotLabel->\"Frequency domain\" ]\n} // Column ", 
    "Display" -> "codemirror", "Hash" -> 
     "5b2ec8aa-f748-4c26-8f31-aabf3bad4b43", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"InitGroup" -> True|>, 
